    {
      "layer": "geography_territory",
      "tag": "loire_valley_commercial_position",
      "direction": "rise",
      "description": "Anjou controlled the middle Loire, the main route between Atlantic commerce and Parisian markets. The Loire wines produced in the county's heartland and toll revenues from Loire river traffic funded Angevin military ambitions.",
